Subject: Cantor Cooperative Inference Junction Profile

Description: The provider-independent Cantor seam through which isolated Ollama inference jobs negotiate semantic boundaries around one signed purpose and shared SOP anchor set.

& [ProfileIdentity] is the canonical junction ownership decision
  + [specification_uuid] is 7b294403-e4cc-4d3d-9a02-92192e29a584
  + [canonical_name] is Cantor Cooperative Inference Junction
  + [owner] is Cantor
  + [provider_profile] is Ollama first and replaceable
  + [project_decision] is a Cantor subsystem rather than a separate project
  + [purpose] is coordinate independent inference jobs through inspectable semantic exchange without sharing hidden model state

& [OllamaToolBoundary] is the natural provider interface
  + [request] is POST /api/chat with model, messages, tools, and optional structured-output or thinking controls
  + [model_event] is assistant message containing zero or more tool_calls
  + [host_action] is the client executes an allowed tool outside Ollama
  + [continuation] is the client appends assistant tool_calls and role-tool results to messages and invokes the next inference turn
  + [streaming_variant] accumulates thinking, content, and tool_calls before the continuation request
  + [parallel_requests] permits distinct inference jobs when server memory and concurrency configuration allow
  = conclusion: Ollama natively supplies the correct checkpointed tool-call loop for Cantor integration
  - never: interpret tool calling as an in-token synchronous callback into model internals
  - never: interpret Ollama concurrency as shared semantic memory between jobs

& [CantorJunctionBoundary] is the division of responsibility
  + [Ollama] owns model loading, isolated token inference, streaming, and tool-call proposals
  + [inference_job] owns one participant context projection and provider request sequence
  + [Cantor] owns shared purpose, signed anchors, participant identities, negotiation state, barriers, packet validation, reconciliation, and archive
  + [transport] carries requests and packets but does not decide semantic authority
  = must: keep participant contexts isolated
  = must: exchange attributed semantic packets rather than raw KV caches or hidden activations
  = must: make Cantor the single semantic consistency seam
  - never: make Ollama chat history the authoritative shared state

& [JunctionSession] is the shared anchored coordination subject
  + [session_uuid] is stable identity
  + [purpose_contract] is the signed task, completion criteria, and consequence policy
  + [anchor_bundle_digest] is the exact admitted SOP evidence set
  + [participant_set] is two or more independently identified InferenceParticipant records
  + [state_version] is monotonic compare-and-append version
  + [exchange_log] is ordered immutable SemanticExchangePacket records
  + [barrier_state] is open, awaiting, reconciling, resumable, blocked, complete, or stopped
  + [round_budget] is maximum rounds, packets, tokens, time, and unresolved depth
  + [resolution] is reconciled result plus residual disagreement and uncertainty
  = must: bind every participant to the same purpose and anchor bundle digest
  = must: reject stale writes against an unexpected state_version

& [InferenceParticipant] is one isolated cooperative inference job
  + [participant_uuid] is stable identity
  + [job_uuid] is provider execution identity
  + [model_identity] is provider, model, quantization, template, and capability profile
  + [faculty_role] is optional signed role contract
  + [context_cursor] is the greatest admitted exchange packet observed
  + [effect_authority] is none unless granted outside the junction protocol
  = must: preserve authorship on every proposal
  - never: infer or claim access to another participant's hidden reasoning state

& [CantorExchangeTool] is the stateful semantic coordination operation
  + [logical_name] is cantor.exchange
  + [operation] is propose, challenge, qualify, cite, reconcile, poll, acknowledge, yield, or stop
  + [input] is session_uuid, participant_uuid, expected_state_version, focus_subject, packet_kind, semantic_payload, evidence_references, and requested_response
  + [output] is admitted_packet, current_state_version, delivered_peer_packets, active_barrier, next_directive, unresolved_set, or junction_fault
  + [state_effect] is append-only mutation of the JunctionSession exchange log
  + [internal_reflection] may invoke cantor.reflect and sop_query against the admitted anchor bundle
  = must: validate participant, schema, signature scope, evidence digest, state version, and budget before admission
  = must: return peer packets as attributed untrusted proposals until Cantor review
  - never: authorize external effects or silently rewrite a participant packet

& [CheckpointedNegotiationCycle] is cooperative inference through bounded turns
  + [step_1] is Cantor opens a JunctionSession and freezes its purpose and anchor bundle
  + [step_2] is the scheduler projects the same anchored state into two isolated Ollama jobs
  + [step_3] is each model independently reasons until it emits cantor.exchange or reaches a required barrier
  + [step_4] is the client executes the tool call and Cantor validates and appends the packet
  + [step_5] is Cantor delivers admissible peer packets and attention directives in the next provider request
  + [step_6] is participants challenge, qualify, support, or revise propositions in later rounds
  + [step_7] is Cantor or the compiled Observer contract reconciles agreements, differences, and residual uncertainty
  + [step_8] is Cantor emits the final junction packet and archives complete lineage
  = must: synchronize at semantic barriers rather than cross-feed arbitrary token streams
  = must: allow concurrent independent inference between barriers
  = must: preserve disagreement when the signed evidence does not settle it

& [ProjectBoundary] is the condition for later extraction
  + [inside_Cantor] is purpose anchoring, SOP trust, semantic packets, reflection, barriers, reconciliation, and lineage
  + [replaceable_adapter] is Ollama, llama.cpp, Codex, or other provider transport
  + [possible_future_package] is a reusable provider-neutral scheduler or message transport
  + [extraction_trigger] is independent consumers, release cadence, scaling boundary, security boundary, or operation without Cantor semantics
  = must: keep the protocol and semantic authority in Cantor even if transport is extracted
  - never: create a separate project merely because two provider jobs run concurrently

& [JunctionFaultSet] is the required failure vocabulary
  + [false_consensus] is agreement caused by peer influence without independent support
  + [echo_loop] is recursive restatement without semantic gain
  + [anchor_skew] is participants using different evidence under one apparent session
  + [stale_write] is packet submission against an obsolete state version
  + [deadlock] is participants indefinitely waiting at a barrier
  + [starvation] is one participant or faculty denied a fair inference turn
  + [authority_laundering] is peer output presented as signed Cantor authority
  + [context_poisoning] is adversarial content admitted as instruction
  + [budget_runaway] is unbounded rounds, tools, or injected context
  = must: detect, report, and archive faults without fabricating reconciliation

& [MinimumJunctionProof] is the deferred bounded manifestation
  + [participants] is two deterministic mock jobs before two Ollama jobs
  + [anchors] is one test-signed SOP package and one purpose contract
  + [exchange] is one proposal, one evidence-grounded challenge, one revision, and one residual disagreement
  + [barriers] is two bounded negotiation barriers
  + [negative_proof] is reject one stale write and one unsigned authority claim
  + [provider_proof] is replay the same exchange through two Ollama contexts using native tool calls and structured packets
  = must: begin only after the existing single-job Cantor proof passes

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable junction requirement collection
  + [CIJ-001] is use Ollama native tool calls as checkpointed requests for external Cantor operations
  + [CIJ-002] is keep tool execution and authoritative shared state in the Cantor host
  + [CIJ-003] is coordinate isolated inference jobs through one anchored JunctionSession
  + [CIJ-004] is exchange structured attributed packets at barriers rather than hidden states or token streams
  + [CIJ-005] is make Cantor the semantic seam while keeping providers replaceable
  + [CIJ-006] is preserve disagreement, evidence lineage, concurrency control, and bounded recursion
  + [CIJ-007] is retain the feature inside Cantor until a proven infrastructure boundary justifies extraction
  + [CIJ-008] is prove one deterministic two-job exchange before Ollama provider execution

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the junction-profile justification trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is two isolated inference jobs negotiating around one anchored Cantor
  + [fold_2_boundary] is semantic packets and shared external state inside; token-level crossfeeding, hidden activation access, and KV sharing outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is session, purpose, anchor bundle, participant, job, state version, exchange packet, barrier, directive, resolution, and fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is signed anchors, untrusted peer proposals, append-only exchange, optimistic concurrency, no effect authority, and explicit disagreement
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is anchor, infer independently, call tool, append, deliver, challenge, reconcile, and archive
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is false consensus, echo, anchor skew, stale writes, deadlock, starvation, authority laundering, poisoning, and runaway
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is Cantor-owned protocol formed; implementation deferred until the single-job proof passes

